<title>GREECE: GREEK PM TO OUTLINE ECON POLICY IN SALONIKA FAIR.</title>
<headline>GREEK PM TO OUTLINE ECON POLICY IN SALONIKA FAIR.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek Prime Minister Costas Simitis will outline his government's plans on the economy at the openning of the international trade fair in Salonika on September 7, Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou said.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be  a speech on the government's work in the economy and giving the perspective for the future,&quot; Papandoniou said a meeting with Simitis and Finance Minister Alexandros Papadopoulos.</p>
<p>Papandoniou has said the economy &quot;is the government's strong card,&quot; for the September 22 snap vote.</p>
<p>--Costas Paris, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
